  "prefLabel": "Env-Wq 1502.65 Steep slope project",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wq 1502.65 “Steep slope project” means a project that involves earth moving activities within the protected shoreland, except those activities associated with public utility lines and associated structures and facilities, public roads, and public water access facilities, that result in a temporary or permanent disturbance of an area that:\n\n(a) Is more than 2,500 square feet in size;\n\n(b) Any portion is within 50 feet of the reference line, as defined in RSA 483-B:4, XVII;\n\n(c) Is sloped such that runoff is in the direction of the surface water; and\n\n(d) Has an existing average grade of 25% or greater over a distance of 50 feet measured in an upgradient direction from a starting point anywhere within 50 feet of the reference line and the area of disturbance.\n\nSource. #14656, eff 8-6-26, EXPIRES: 8-6-36",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wq1500.html"
}
